#X text -3 222 -autobw that calculate the bw of a formant according to its frequency, f 44;
#X text -3 259 -autoamp and fcomp \, the scariest of the gang \, that calculates amplitude according to the frequencies and bw of all formants \, in a big matrix that includes an additionnal \, compensative non sounding formant at 80hz, f 44;
#X text -3 334 -chpcont \, that reduce amp according to the frequency, f 44;
#X text -2 508 it then goes to 5 formants generators and into your out~, f 92;
#X text -3 148 then the voice parameters go in the autorule part that contains :, f 93;
#X text -3 185 -auto bend that bends the first 2 formants frequencies depending on the base frequency, f 44;
#X text -2 622 PS: my starting idea was to synthesise a choire \, tell me if you think its realistic or not \, cpu-wise, f 92;
#X text -2 535 there is still autotex and spcor to create \, they have to do with skirtwidh but i did not really go into that, f 92;
#X text -3 371 -cslope \, that calculates final amp according to f \, amp and the ton of parameters on the top left (note cslope1 differs from the others), f 22;
#X text 258 383 i stopped at cslope bc its not working \, and it was maybe the limits of my math \, so i have an approximate and ugly vowels generator. thanks me later :*, f 27;
